As a kid, I played Hack in the mid 80s on a home PC and never got
anywhere (my record was probably DL 8).
In the early 90s, I discovered nethack (at university).  I survived a
little bit longer, but still didn't even come close to finding the
castle.
In May, I stumbled across nethackwiki.com, and decided to give the
game another go.
After one wizard-mode dry run and a couple of failures, I'm pleased to
report that I finally ascended some 25 years after I first tried out
this game.  Many thanks to the wiki, without which this ascension
would not have been possible.

You might be interested in my 2 failures:
1) Dipping for Excalibur spawned a water demon that summoned Yeenoghu
who paralyzed me before I realized that even with 80 HP and AC -1,
Elbereth was necessary.
2) early poison instakill.

I got Excalibur out of the 4th fountain I tried.  I chose to do
Sokoban first, found the Oracle on DL 6, and got my AoR out of the zoo
without incident.  Unfortunately, somehow I didn't find a single
unicorn during Sokoban, and was getting awfully nervous about not
having poison resistance. (especialy given my last game's instadeath)
I finally found a cross aligned unicorn on the second level of mines
and took the horn.  I didn't get poison resistance from the corpse,
and I got attacked by killer bees shortly after getting the horn.  Now
that I had the horn, though, I started eating the bee corpses and got
the poison resistance.

In minetown, Izchak had two identical lamps, so I figured they were
probably oil lamps without bothering to look up the price.  I rubbed
one anyway just for fun.  and then the djinni granted me a wish!  I
paid the usage fee and bought the 2nd lamp (why is the usage fee
higher?).  The 2nd lamp was blessed and gave me a 2nd wish, so I got a
BoH and GDSM from the two lamps.  As soon as I got my GDSM, I started
wondering if I should have gotten a cloak of magic resistance
instead.  My Mithril coat was reasonable armor, and I think would have
done fine until I got SDSM from the castle wand.  Regardless, I then
bought protection with the fruits of credit cloning, price ID'd a
bunch of stuff, and got my luckstone out of Mines' End.

I max'ed out my luck with sacrifices, set up a stash in Sokoban, and
started exploring the rest of the dungeons.  Fort Ludios gave me an
oilskin cloak just before I wandered next to an eel in the moat (I
didn't have a light on).  It also gave me a [cursed] ring of
levitation, which was good because I was starting to get nervous about
how to get navigate Medusa's island.  The quest was easy enough, and
thanks to a tinning kit, I left with strength around 18/95.  I had
enough potion by now to use alchemy to make 7 blessed gain abilities,
so I was able to max out all of my stats.  (jumping in water to dilute
potions is so much more annoying than water walking boots).

On my way to the castle, a Master-Lich attacked, and I didn't have a
scroll of genocide yet.  I hit it once, and it warped away.  I started
making a beeline for the downstairs, and then a wave of psychic energy
found me.  Great:  a Master Lich and a mind flayer and no scrolls of
genocide.  I left the level, but when I later came back, they were
gone.  must have been a shapeshifter?

I made my way down to the castle, collected a bunch of stuff, and then
decided to go back to my stash to polypile before using my new wand of
wishing(0:1).  After invoking the Orb of Fate, I realized that I still
didn't have teleport control.  So, I decided to start kicking sinks.
I only found 3 sinks in all the dungeons, and they didn't give me
anything useful.  I had about 20 rings to polypile with, though, so I
figured I could eventually get what I wanted.  I had seen a few tengu
around so I crossed my fingers, and killed the first one.  I was glad
when it left a corpse.  I was not glad when eating it made me jumpy.
The next two didn't leave corpses, and now I really needed that =oTC.

Polypiling used up almost all of my rings before giving me that =oTC.
I did get a wand of cancellation from the wands, which helped uncurse
a lot of the elven cloaks and boots.  These then yielded a cloak of
magic resistance, helm of brilliance, helm of telepathy, and water
walking boots.  The last 3 scrolls that I got were some of the most
useful:  charging, enchant armor, and enchant weapon.  No magic
markers from the magic tools.  :-(
So, I wished for a magic marker, GoP, speed boots, and a T-shirt.  I
saved the "last" wish for later.  I made some SDSM from some silver
scales, and then felt much safer wearing my "oLS.

With hundreds of HP, and AC of -35, Gehennom was mostly uneventful.
One major goof was clearing out the Wizard's Tower before my ascension
run.  I used an oilskin cloak while fighting the sea monsters, but
forgot to go back to the cloak of magic resistance.  Wandering around
in Gehennom later, I triggered a polymorph trap which destroyed my +5
T-shirt and oilskin cloak.  :-(  I thought I had also destroyed my +4
SDSM, but I guess that comes back when you revert to human form.
phew.

Using a wand of digging and wand of death, I killed Rodney without
waking him up, performed the invokation and entered Moloch's Sanctum
with a ring of conflict.  I had 3 wands of death with 11 charges
between them, so I figured I could afford to use a couple charges in
the sanctum.  A single charge took out 3 priests and a demon, the
other charge took out the high priest.  Twoweapon with a +7 Excalibur
and +7 silver saber took care of other monsters that got in the way.

The mysterious force started off kind and I got up to DL40 nicely,
then it started hammering me, slowly working me back down to DL45.
When Rodney showed up, I tried the /oD again, and it missed 3 times
(is that normal?).  After the 3rd miss, I tried to just hit him out of
frustration.  He then summoned monsters, and I went back to the /oD...
and killed the Elvenking!  I don't think I killed Rodney, but I didn't
see him again for 30 levels or so.  When I did see him again on DL4, I
was able to kill him with a rubber chicken.

After using up my 130 power and 20 scrolls on teleporting, I finally
got to the exit stairs and to the plane of Earth.  I still had the
rubber chicken to take care of Rodney again.  I only had 3 potions of
confusion, so I tried a cursed unicorn horn on the plane of Earth.
After a dozen tries, I was finally confused, but hallucinating as
well.  Reading the scroll like this did find the portal, but marked it
as a potion or something.

The planes weren't a problem at all.  I finished the Plane of Air with
a full 471 HP.  I didn't use a ring of conflict on the Astral Plane.
I tried calling the priests names to find which altar to go for, and
it was defended by Pestilence.  I zapped the /oD at Pestilence, and it
missed... but then bounced off of the priest's medallion and hit him
from behind.  :-)  There were then several priests in front of me, so
I tried zapping a /oT to get them out of the way.  which promptly
revived Pestilence.  oops.  The /oD didn't miss on the next try, and
this time I fought past the corpse before going back to the /oT.  I
got near the door of the temple using up teleport charges, but
accidentally hit the high priest of Tyr with one of the zaps, and I
guess high priests don't like that.  No matter, I just ignored him as
I walked up to the altar and ascended.

405 out of 471 HP when ascending.  AC around -30 (after ripping apart
my T-shirt).  I used about 45k turns, starting 5/22 and ending 6/5.
XP level 30.  Max DL 49.  3.5M points.  blessed genocided Ls, uncursed
genocided MMFs and MFs.

Thanks for humoring my excitement and reading through this long post!

